        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c32b37b7-e4e3-5de8-880a-aab18f6a946a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Beauty and the Beast franchise, Beauty and the Beast (1991 film)\n- People: Gary Trousdale, Kirk Wise, Jeanne-Marie Leprince de Beaumont, Jean Cocteau\n- Concepts: Disney Renaissance, French fairy tales, Broadway musicals\n- Related works: 1946 Beauty and the Beast film, direct-to-video follow-up films, live-action spin-off television series, video games, merchandise\n- Places: Disney World\n\nFacts:\n- Jeanne-Marie Leprince de Beaumont wrote the French fairy tale Beauty and the Beast, which was the basis for Disney's 1991 film, and she was credited in both the English and French versions.\n- Jean Cocteau directed the 1946 French film Beauty and the Beast, whose ideas also influenced Disney's 1991 film.\n- Disney's 1991 animated Beauty and the Beast was the 30th Disney animated feature film and the third film released during the Disney Renaissance.\n- Gary Trousdale and Kirk Wise directed the 1991 American animated feature Beauty and the Beast.\n- The success of Disney's 1991 Beauty and the Beast led to three direct-to-video follow-up films, a live-action spin-off television series, a Disney World stage show, a Disney World restaurant, several video games, merchandise, and a Broadway musical.\n- The Beauty and the Beast Broadway musical became the ninth longest-running musical in Broadway history and received nine Tony Award nominations, winning Best Costume Design.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "585dfb53-a487-5d01-bbab-54f96bad36ff",
        "text": "Page: Beauty and the Beast (franchise). Sentence: The success of the original 1991 American animated feature, \"Beauty and the Beast\", directed by Gary Trousdale and Kirk Wise, led to three direct-to-video follow-up films, a live-action spin-off television series, a Disney World stage show, a Disney World restaurant, several video games, merchandise, and the 9th longest-running musical in Broadway history, which was nominated for nine Tony Awards, winning for Best Costume Design.\nPage: Beauty and the Beast (1991 film). Sentence: The 30th Disney animated feature film and the third released during the Disney Renaissance period, it is based on the French fairy tale of the same name by Jeanne-Marie Leprince de Beaumont (who was also credited in the English version as well as in the French version), and ideas from the 1946 French film of the same name directed by Jean Cocteau.",
